WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.080
The David Pakman Show at David Pakman dot
com.

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:08.060
If you follow politics, if you work in politics,
you report on politics, you generally understand

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:15.059
that every American president through foreign
policy makes decisions that lead to people

00:00:15.059 --> 00:00:16.059
dying.

00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:17.670
It could be a drone strike.

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:21.720
It could be cutting key medical aid to another
country.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.349
It could be sending people to war.

00:00:24.349 --> 00:00:27.279
So through foreign policy.

00:00:27.279 --> 00:00:28.769
Presidents cause death.

00:00:28.769 --> 00:00:31.109
That's not a new thing.

00:00:31.109 --> 00:00:36.530
But the Trump administration has turned deadly
in a way that is different, in a way that

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.520
is much more easily preventable.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:44.360
Elizabeth Drew wrote a really good article
about this for Project Syndicate, and she

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:50.160
points out that the Trump administration has
turned deadly simply because Donald Trump

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:56.410
ignored readily available advice from scientists
and other knowledgeable advisers from day

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.230
one on the issue of Corona virus.

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:04.030
Donald Trump was told about the risks of doing
nothing back in December and January.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:06.260
And now he says, nobody knew.

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:07.690
Nobody could have imagined.

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:15.170
Trump was given the pandemic playbook by the
Obama administration, color coded 69 pages

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:19.890
and ignored it and now says nobody could have
expected this.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:23.230
But we know intelligence agencies were warning
him.

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:25.340
Science agencies were warning him.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:30.070
Public health agencies were telling him what
was potentially coming.

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:32.130
And he also had been briefed.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:38.200
His administration had been briefed by the
outgoing Obama administration in 2017, unexamined

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.670
daily, how to deal with a pandemic.

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:43.880
And Trump never focused on it, and he always
ignored it.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:45.560
He dismissed the virus.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:48.390
He said it wouldn't be worse than the flu.

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:51.740
He said we had 15 cases, which would soon
be zero.

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:53.600
He bragged that nobody had died.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:55.250
He said it's under control.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:59.590
And of course, it was all wrong and it has
been deadly.

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:07.200
Trump could have just not invoked but utilized
the Defense Production Act a while ago to

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:10.479
force the production of much needed medical
supplies.

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:16.920
But he was successfully lobbied by the Chamber
of Commerce and Industry not to do that.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:20.770
And so he waited and waited and we fell further
and further behind.

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:25.819
He didn't mobilize the federal stockpile of
ventilators and other supplies.

00:02:25.819 --> 00:02:31.880
Later, having his son in law, Jared Kushner,
claim in dystopian fashion that the stockpile

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:34.860
is ours, not the states.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:42.349
In a very sinister, ominous press briefing
last Thursday and all of this led to far more

00:02:42.349 --> 00:02:44.340
death than necessary.

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:48.020
Trump played favorites with states regularly.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:52.349
We get reports that red state governors were
getting everything they asked for in terms

00:02:52.349 --> 00:02:54.349
of supplies and equipment.

00:02:54.349 --> 00:03:01.220
While many blue state governors were not and
Trump continued and continues to blame systems

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:04.660
he inherited, which is code for blame Obama.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:11.349
Trump is negotiating in some cases against
states for medical supplies that those states

00:03:11.349 --> 00:03:15.680
need, while insisting states have to go out
and get their stuff and blaming states for

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.740
shortages that they experience.

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:23.459
Trump is regularly using war language to try
to weaponize the virus as a political tool

00:03:23.459 --> 00:03:24.900
for reelection.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:31.280
And so the decisions that he makes have always
been primarily influenced by political calculations

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:32.810
and political expediency.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:35.510
And in the background of all of this.

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:40.569
We hear lame economic arguments made, which
essentially are arguments that say it's OK

00:03:40.569 --> 00:03:44.000
for more people should die in exchange for
the economy.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.670
The economy is meant to be open.

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:47.450
The country is meant to be open.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:51.100
The cure cannot be worse than the disease
or we can't allow it to be worse than the

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.100
disease.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:58.100
And of course, this ignores the reality that
from day one, if we had had a proper six week

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:04.330
shutdown, we would have prevented the need
for these overlapping partial shutdowns that

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:09.970
still are going to do economic damage, but
won't actually fix the problem once and for

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:10.970
all.

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:15.239
It's almost impossible to do a worse job than
Donald Trump did.

00:04:15.239 --> 00:04:19.909
Many small business owners I know people who
just run a restaurant would have been able

00:04:19.909 --> 00:04:22.259
to manage this better than Donald Trump.

00:04:22.259 --> 00:04:27.039
Given all of the resources that he had at
his disposal, many of which he chose to ignore.

00:04:27.039 --> 00:04:33.629
And if you want to play the business game,
any modest, humble, you know, professor I

00:04:33.629 --> 00:04:38.580
had in business school would have been able
to manage this better than Donald Trump, because

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:42.650
most of peop- most people who who actually
understand business and are good at business

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:47.470
understand the importance of deferring to
experts, which Donald Trump seems essentially

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:48.849
unable to do.

00:04:48.849 --> 00:04:54.550
Any doctor who runs a medical practice would
have managed this better than Donald Trump.

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:59.400
If Trump had done nothing other than to say
I'm appointing a.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:04.909
Corona virus czar like Ronald Clain, maybe
Barack Obama's Ebola czar.

00:05:04.909 --> 00:05:06.629
And just let them handle that.

00:05:06.629 --> 00:05:08.449
Let them handle it and stayed out of it.

00:05:08.449 --> 00:05:10.289
We would be far better off.

00:05:10.289 --> 00:05:14.539
So, yes, presidents lead to death through
foreign policy and through domestic policy

00:05:14.539 --> 00:05:16.330
and a lot of different ways.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:22.270
But the Trump presidency has now become deadly
in a way that is very different than what

00:05:22.270 --> 00:05:27.729
we normally say when we say presidents lead
to death through foreign policy.

00:05:27.729 --> 00:05:29.449
It's very, very ugly and we don't yet know
how bad it's going to get.

